 ## Operating characteristics
-Time complexity is $O(n^2)$ for an $n \times n$ grid. Memory complexity is $O(n^2)$ for the height lattice and vertex arrays. Performance depends on the cost of `heightAt`, `slopeAt`, and `surface` calls. Strengths include efficient generation of large, distant terrain views with consistent shading. Limitations include the coarse resolution suitable only for far terrain, not detailed close-up geometry. Use for background terrain rendering; not for interactive close-up terrain modification.
